    "body": "Direct answer on the vehicle LOW/NORMAL result: the current source submits the same LOW/NORMAL boolean every eligible vehicle frame, so this is not the old one-frame reset bug. The installed result shows that the vehicle follow camera ignores that on-foot/horse framing native. Current 1491.50 Story scripts contain no vehicle call to it and no proved vehicle LOW equivalent; the separate vehicle-camera native selects a vehicle camera state but its numeric states are not a proved LOW/NORMAL mapping. I will not guess those values. This is a limitation of the known binary LOW native in the vehicle rig, not proof that every possible vehicle-camera implementation is impossible. Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#108 stays actionable.",
